+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders, especially a switch to email to save money. Pickup
+reminders go by SMS because the April–June 2025 email trial coincided with more missed pickups and wasted fresh
+food. This page preserves the reasons after volunteers proposed email for the third time in a year.
+
+## Behavior
+
+Members receive a reminder of their pickup slot the day before. The
+[reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) selects the channel and sends the message.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+The April–June 2025 email trial left 34% of reminder emails unopened, according to the provider's report quoted in
+[issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md). Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a
+packed bag whose fresh food went in the bin at closing time. The pantry lead reported that many members share one
+phone in the family and never check email, but do see SMS.
+
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025; missed pickups were back to 6% by August. In the September
+discussion, email was proposed again because it was free while SMS cost €40 a month. The maintainer confirmed the
+choice to keep SMS on September 8.
+
+Email would remove the SMS bill, but the trial showed that it failed to reach many members and accompanied more
+missed pickups and food waste. Keeping SMS accepts the reported €40 monthly cost to reach those members and retain
+the lower observed missed-pickup rate. That is the trade-off to revisit before proposing email again.
